<section class="view eval-workspace" data-panel="evaluation" aria-labelledby="evalTitle" hidden>
  <div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE · BEHAVIOUR · REGRESSION</div><h1 id="evalTitle">LLM evaluation</h1><p>Run reviewed scenarios against selected, recorded model targets. Separate executable checks, human judgement and paper-trading results.</p></div>
  <div class="surface panel-pad eval-notice" id="evalAccess"><p>Managed email sign-in is required. Wallet-only sessions cannot run evaluations or change policy.</p><button type="button" class="button button-primary" id="evalSignIn">Sign in</button></div>
  <div id="evalWorkspace" hidden>
    <div class="eval-toolbar"><span class="status-tag" id="evalNodeState">Not loaded</span><span id="evalQuota" class="context-hint"></span><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalRefresh">Refresh</button></div>
    <div id="evalStatus" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="eval-status"></div>
    <nav class="eval-tabs" aria-label="Evaluation workspace">
      <button type="button" class="button button-outline" data-eval-tab="runs" aria-pressed="true">Runs &amp; results</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-outline" data-eval-tab="datasets" aria-pressed="false">Datasets &amp; coverage</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-outline" data-eval-tab="reviews" aria-pressed="false">Review queue</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-outline" data-eval-tab="account" aria-pressed="false">Account settings</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-outline" data-eval-tab="node" id="evalNodeTab" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Node policy</button>
    </nav>
    <div data-eval-pane="runs">
      <section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Start a comparison</h2><p class="context-hint">Each target receives the same selected cases and generation limits. Gold checks and future market data stay outside the model request. The account settings below select targets and repetitions.</p>
        <form id="evalRunForm" class="stack-form"><div class="field-grid">
          <label>Reviewed suite<select id="evalRunSuite" required></select></label>
          <label>Dataset split<select id="evalSplit"><option value="dev">Development</option><option value="test">Test</option><option value="holdout">Holdout</option></select></label>
        </div><label>Idempotency key<input id="evalRunKey" maxlength="128" required autocomplete="off"></label>
        <div class="inline-actions"><button type="submit" class="button button-primary" id="evalRunSubmit">Run evaluation</button><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalNewKey">New run key</button></div>
        <p class="context-hint">A timeout does not mean a request was free or never ran. Reuse this key to resolve submission uncertainty. No automatic paid retries.</p></form>
      </section>
      <section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Run history</h2><div id="evalRunList" class="eval-table-wrap"></div></section>
      <section class="surface panel-pad" id="evalReportPanel" hidden><div class="panel-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">PINNED SUITE · OBSERVED OUTCOMES</div><h2 id="evalReportTitle">Run report</h2></div><span class="status-tag" id="evalGate"></span></div>
        <div id="evalMetrics" class="eval-metrics"></div><div class="inline-actions"><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalEvidence">Export integrity receipt</button><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalCancel">Cancel remaining work</button></div>
        <p class="context-hint">Pass rates use all planned trials, including errors and interruptions. A critical failure blocks the gate. Citation checks validate reference IDs, not semantic truth. Trading is paper replay only.</p>
        <h3>Target scorecards</h3><div id="evalTargets" class="eval-table-wrap"></div>
        <h3>Failure explorer</h3><label>Outcome filter<select id="evalOutcomeFilter"><option value="all">All outcomes</option><option value="not_pass">Not passing</option><option value="indeterminate">Needs review</option><option value="uncertain">Uncertain request</option></select></label><div id="evalCases" class="eval-table-wrap"></div>
        <h3>Recommendations and slice metrics</h3><pre id="evalFindings" class="code-display"></pre>
        <details><summary>Selected trial: input, output and check evidence</summary><pre id="evalTrial" class="code-display">Choose Inspect on a trial.</pre></details>
      </section>
      <section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Paired regression comparison</h2><form id="evalCompareForm" class="stack-form"><div class="field-grid"><label>Baseline run ID<input id="evalBaseline" required></label><label>Baseline target ID<input id="evalBaselineTarget" required></label><label>Candidate run ID<input id="evalCandidate" required></label><label>Candidate target ID<input id="evalCandidateTarget" required></label></div><button class="button button-outline" type="submit">Compare identical cases</button></form><pre id="evalComparison" class="code-display">Same suite and split required. Incomplete pairs remain visible.</pre></section>
    </div>
    <div data-eval-pane="datasets" hidden>
      <section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Versioned evaluation datasets</h2><p class="context-hint">Import cases, fixed references, executable checks and anchored human rubrics. Editing any gold label, reference, reviewer list or case creates a new content-addressed suite. Explicit reviewer IDs grant access to that suite and its trials.</p>
        <div class="inline-actions"><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalLoadDialogue">Load synthetic dialogue example</button><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="evalLoadTrading">Load paper-trading example</button><label>Import JSON file<input id="evalDatasetFile" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label></div>
        <form id="evalImportForm" class="stack-form"><label>Suite JSON, maximum 2 MiB<textarea id="evalDatasetInput" class="code-input" rows="16" required spellcheck="false"></textarea></label><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Validate &amp; save new snapshot</button></form><p class="context-hint">Examples are synthetic smoke tests, not production benchmarks. Review sampling, annotation quality and leakage before using a suite as a release gate.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Coverage &amp; annotation approval</h2><div id="evalSuiteList" class="eval-table-wrap"></div><pre id="evalSuiteDetail" class="code-display">Inspect a suite to see its source, frozen references and annotation guidelines.</pre>
        <form id="evalApproveForm" class="stack-form"><label>Suite hash<input id="evalApproveId" required></label><label>Review notes<textarea id="evalApproveNote" rows="3" maxlength="4096" required></textarea></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="evalApproveChecked" required> I reviewed the labels, coverage, provenance and split assignments.</label><button class="button button-outline" type="submit">Record my annotation approval</button></form>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div data-eval-pane="reviews" hidden><section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Independent review queue</h2><p class="context-hint">Only explicitly authorized reviewers can inspect or rate a shared suite. Trial views omit other reviewers’ votes and provider identity. Votes are immutable and disagreements remain indeterminate.</p><div id="evalReviewList" class="eval-table-wrap"></div><pre id="evalReviewDetail" class="code-display">Choose a review item.</pre><form id="evalReviewForm" class="stack-form"><label>Verdict<select id="evalReviewVerdict"><option value="pass">Pass</option><option value="fail">Fail</option><option value="indeterminate">Indeterminate</option></select></label><label>Evidence and reasoning<textarea id="evalReviewNote" rows="4" maxlength="4096" required></textarea></label><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Record review</button></form></section></div>
    <div data-eval-pane="account" hidden><section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Account evaluation settings</h2><p class="context-hint">These preferences affect this account on this node. Node allowlists and ceilings always take precedence. Credentials stay in the existing server-side model configuration.</p><form id="evalAccountForm" class="stack-form"><div id="evalAccountFields" class="field-grid"></div><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Save account settings</button></form><h3>Effective settings</h3><pre id="evalEffective" class="code-display"></pre></section></div>
    <div data-eval-pane="node" hidden><section class="surface panel-pad"><h2>Node-wide evaluation policy</h2><p class="context-hint">The same versioned fields appear under DamageBDD → Node administration → ECAI settings → LLM evaluation. Defaults disable evaluation and remote inference. Changes are persisted by the existing node settings service.</p><form id="evalNodeForm" class="stack-form"><div id="evalNodeFields" class="field-grid"></div><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Save node policy</button></form><p class="context-hint">Target IDs must refer to explicitly configured code_model_nodes or code_ollama_nodes entries. Remote targets require verified TLS. Limits cover this node; they are not a cross-node or currency budget.</p></section></div>
  </div>
</section>
